ted, axis -4.0 to 1.0; the curves are drawn from about -3.14 to about 0.86. Printed 'Log H Ref: -1.14'.","Spectral sensitivity: effective exposure 1/50 s, density 0.2 above D-min, Status M; y is log sensitivity (reciprocal exposure in erg/cm2) as printed, and on this sheet the axis runs -1.0 to 3.0 (not 0.0 to 4.0). The yellow-forming (b) curve starts at about 375 nm, the magenta-forming (g) at about 395 nm, the cyan-forming (r) at about 485 nm and ends at about 695 nm; the g curve has a blue shoulder (about 0.7 to 0.9) before its green peak.","Spectral-dye-density plot has only 'Midscale Density' (mid, drawn dashed; the sheet labels it 'Midscale Density' here) and 'Minimum Density' (min), no separate c/m/y dyes; the dashed curve is read through its dashes. Both curves start at 400 nm already high (mid about 1.9, min about 1.4) and fall steeply.","Printed checks (Status M red-filter densities of a normally exposed negative): grey card 0.80 to 1.00; lightest paper-gray-scale step 1.20 to 1.40. The sheet's modulation transfer function plot is not traced.","Grain: Print Grain Index for 135 at 4x6 print (32); 8x10 = 54, 16x20 = 84. The sheet says the film is optimized for printing on Kodak Professional Portra Endura, Supra Endura and Ultra Endura Papers, Duraflex Plus Digital Display Material and Endura Metallic Paper."],"print":"kodak-endura-premier","grain":{"grain":12.6,"grain_size":26.0,"grain_roughness":50.0}}